    (alert budget 5% of events, momentum lag 3)
====================================================================================================
  h   events   emerged    base   proximity   momentum    ordflow      model   model/best
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1    1,240        48    3.9%        3.2%       8.1%       3.2%       6.5%        0.80x
  2    1,783        89    5.0%        6.7%      11.2%       5.6%      15.7%        1.40x
  3    2,137       117    5.5%        4.7%       6.6%       1.9%      16.0%        2.43x
  6    2,458       125    5.1%        5.7%      11.5%       3.3%      16.4%        1.43x
 12    2,491       115    4.6%        8.1%       7.3%       0.8%      18.5%        2.30x
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  proximity = rank by the stale gap (closest to crossing). Model-free.
  momentum  = rank by gap(t) - gap(t-lag). Model-free.
  ordflow   = rank by net_flow(B) - net_flow(A), the SIGNED order-flow
              imbalance already in the feature vector (slot 5). This is
              'predict where order flow momentum is heading', done with
              arithmetic. It is the hardest baseline here.
  model/best = model precision divided by the BEST of the three baselines.
               Beating the base rate is not enough; beat the obvious rules.

  Bootstrap at h=12 (2000 resamples, budget 124):
    model / best baseline   5th 1.40x   median 2.18x   95th 3.43x
    -> interval excludes 1.0 UPWARD: the model anticipates emergences
       that proximity, price momentum and raw ORDER FLOW all miss.
       THIS is predictive arbitrage, and it is the project's claim.
  Per-series at h=12 (>=150 events, >=8 emergences):
    series                  events  emerg    base    prox     mom    flow   model   m/best
    KXHURCAT                   443     12    2.7%    0.0%    0.0%    0.0%    4.5%     nanx
    KXBTCD                     268     88   32.8%   46.2%   30.8%   15.4%   61.5%    1.33x
    -> compare the SAME family across splits. A family present in only
       one split cannot be replicated there, and its absence is not
       evidence against the model.


